[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: GHOST MCP Capabilities and Memory Requirements
UID: GHOST-MCP-CAPABILITIES
VERSION: 0.1-draft
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text
  AUTO_LEVELS: On
  NODE_IN_TOC: True

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Purpose and Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the approved GHOST MCP functional capabilities other than ActiveBlackboard.

It owns:

1. Prompt Engineering.
2. Episodic Memory.
3. Clipboard Memory.
4. Collection Memory.
5. Shared memory Save, Recall, List, and Delete semantics applicable to these modes.

All current implementation and future requirements concerning ActiveBlackboard or Persistent Chat belong exclusively to 112_mcp_activeblackboard.sdoc.

The memory requirements in this document extend GHOST through MCP without requiring a broad rewrite of the established 50-series Memory Management baseline.

Where the existing core Memory Management infrastructure is reused, its existing requirements remain valid for their original scope.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CAP-ROOT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: MCP Capability Scope
STATEMENT: >>>
GHOST MCP shall support the approved Prompt Engineering capability and three non-ActiveBlackboard memory modes:

- Episodic Memory;
- Clipboard Memory; and
- Collection Memory.

ActiveBlackboard shall remain separately owned by 112_mcp_activeblackboard.sdoc.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. Prompt Engineering

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Prompt Engineering is an already implemented GHOST MCP capability.

Temporary experimental client-routing forms, including current Prompt:, MEM:, or plain-request mode experiments, are not stabilized as requirements by this document.

The durable requirement is the GHOST prompt-engineering capability itself.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-ENGINEER-PROMPT-TOOL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: GHOST Prompt Engineering Tool
STATEMENT: >>>
The MCP server shall expose the GHOST Prompt Engineering capability through the tool identifier:

ghost_engineer_prompt

The tool shall use the established GHOST prompt-processing path rather than implement an independent MCP-specific prompt-engineering algorithm.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CAP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-APPROVED-FLOW
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Prompt Engineering Processing Flow
STATEMENT: >>>
The stable Prompt Engineering processing path shall:

1. accept the current prompt text;
2. create isolated request state;
3. execute existing deterministic PreProcessing;
4. execute existing A2 PromptShaper on the resulting SuperPrompt;
5. rebuild the authoritative prompt-ready representation; and
6. return the engineered prompt.

Prompt Engineering shall not independently duplicate PreProcessing or A2 algorithms inside the MCP adapter.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ENGINEER-PROMPT-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-FRESH-SUPERPROMPT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Fresh Prompt State Per Prompt-Engineering Call
STATEMENT: >>>
Each Prompt Engineering call shall operate on request-isolated SuperPrompt state.

Mutable prompt state from another user, request, or earlier tool call shall not be reused as the active processing state for the new call.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-APPROVED-FLOW

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PREPROCESS-CALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Existing PreProcessing Reuse
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Engineering adapter shall invoke the existing GHOST deterministic PreProcessing behavior.

It shall not implement a second MCP-specific parser, canonical-header model, default system, alias model, or prompt normalization algorithm.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-APPROVED-FLOW

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PREPROCESS-STAGE-GATE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: PreProcessing Completion Gate
STATEMENT: >>>
A2 PromptShaper shall execute only after successful completion of the required PreProcessing operation for the same request.

A failed PreProcessing operation shall not be represented as a successful engineered prompt.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PREPROCESS-CALL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-A2-CALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Existing A2 PromptShaper Reuse
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Engineering capability shall invoke the established A2 PromptShaper behavior and its existing Agent Stack infrastructure.

The MCP adapter shall not create a second independent A2 prompt, selector implementation, field-write-back algorithm, or provider-specific A2 pipeline.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PREPROCESS-STAGE-GATE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-A2-COMPLETION-GATE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: A2 Completion Gate
STATEMENT: >>>
A successful engineered-prompt result shall be produced only after the required A2 processing and final prompt projection have completed successfully.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-A2-CALL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-ENGINEERED-PROMPT-SOURCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Authoritative Engineered Prompt Source
STATEMENT: >>>
The engineered prompt returned through MCP shall originate from the authoritative GHOST prompt-ready projection.

The MCP adapter shall not independently regenerate or paraphrase that engineered prompt.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-A2-COMPLETION-GATE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-NO-ANSWER-GENERATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Prompt Engineering Is Not Answer Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The ghost_engineer_prompt operation itself shall remain a prompt-engineering capability.

Its core GHOST operation shall not be redefined as the application's general final-answer generator.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ENGINEER-PROMPT-TOOL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PROMPT-EXPERIMENT-BOUNDARY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Experimental Prompt Modes Are Not Stable Requirements
STATEMENT: >>>
Temporary implementation experiments that alter client behavior around ghost_engineer_prompt, including experimental Prompt:, MEM:, plain-request mode switching or supportive-context routing, shall not become stable product requirements unless separately approved.

Their temporary presence in source code shall not require preservation in future MCP implementations.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ENGINEER-PROMPT-TOOL

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. MCP Memory Model

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Four-Mode MCP Memory Model
STATEMENT: >>>
The approved GHOST MCP memory model shall consist of four conceptual memory modes:

1. Episodic Memory.
2. Clipboard Memory.
3. Collection Memory.
4. ActiveBlackboard Memory.

This document owns the first three modes.

ActiveBlackboard is owned exclusively by 112_mcp_activeblackboard.sdoc.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CAP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-COMMON-TRUTH
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Common Durable Memory Infrastructure
STATEMENT: >>>
MCP memory modes may reuse the established GHOST durable-memory infrastructure, including:

- MemoryRecord;
- .ragmem durable episode bodies;
- .ragmeta.json metadata;
- SQLite indexing; and
- vector storage where required by the owning memory mode.

MCP-specific semantics shall not require creation of a second unrelated memory truth model when the common GHOST infrastructure can represent the approved behavior.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-OWNER-SCOPE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Owner-Scoped Memory
STATEMENT: >>>
Every persistent MCP memory operation shall be scoped to the authenticated owner.

An exact key, record ID, Collection ID, Collection Name, Clipboard slot, or other selector shall never bypass owner isolation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-COMMON-TRUTH

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Shared Memory Operations

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.1. Save

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-SAVE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Shared Save Concept
STATEMENT: >>>
GHOST shall expose one clear Save concept for ordinary memory episodes.

The current executable tool identifier ghost_memory_tag represents the existing implementation of this save concept.

A future rename of that tool is not approved by this requirement and shall require a separate interface-contract decision.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-SAVE-VISIBLE-CONTENT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Save Visible Conversation Content
STATEMENT: >>>
When saving a visible conversation episode, the selected visible user content and corresponding visible assistant content shall be stored without substitution by hidden reasoning, internal tool traffic, or an internal model/tool result.

When exact visible content is required by the selected Save operation, ChatGPT shall pass that content without summarizing it.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-SAVE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-SAVE-TITLE-DESCRIPTION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Episode Title and Description
STATEMENT: >>>
A newly saved ordinary memory episode shall have:

- an Episode Title; and
- an Episode Description.

ChatGPT shall generate both from the selected visible episode unless a more specific mode requirement states otherwise.

Episode Title is primarily human-facing metadata.

Episode Description is the compact semantic description used by intelligent Episodic retrieval.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-SAVE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-SAVE-RECALL-KEY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Recall Key Handling
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user explicitly provides a Recall Key, ChatGPT shall pass that key.

When the user requests an Episodic save without providing a Recall Key, ChatGPT shall generate an appropriate Recall Key rather than forcing the user to invent one.

The final duplicate-key collision policy is not fixed by this requirement and shall not be invented here.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-SAVE

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.2. Recall

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-RECALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Shared Recall Concept
STATEMENT: >>>
GHOST shall expose one Recall concept capable of selecting the appropriate retrieval path from the user's request.

For Episodic Memory, Recall shall support:

- deterministic exact retrieval when an exact Recall Key or exact Record ID is known; and
- intelligent semantic retrieval when the user describes a memory without knowing its exact identifier.

The two paths access the same Episodic Memory domain.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-EXACT-RECALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact Recall
STATEMENT: >>>
An exact Recall Key or exact Record ID shall be handled deterministically.

Exact identifiers shall directly select stored records within the authenticated owner's scope.

Exact Recall shall not require semantic vector ranking.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-RECALL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-NO-FAKE-EXACT-FILTER
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact Identifiers Are Not Intelligent-Retrieval Filters
STATEMENT: >>>
Recall Key and Record ID shall not be treated as approximate SQL narrowing filters for intelligent semantic retrieval.

When an exact identifier is supplied, GHOST shall use the deterministic exact path.

When the identifier is unknown, GHOST shall use the intelligent Episodic retrieval path defined in this document.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-RECALL

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.3. List

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-LIST
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Shared Memory List
STATEMENT: >>>
ghost_memory_list shall provide metadata discovery and navigation rather than full episode retrieval.

The shared list capability shall be available for memory modes where listing is meaningful, except Clipboard Memory.

The list capability may return identifying and descriptive metadata such as:

- memory or conversation name;
- memory type;
- Recall Key;
- Record ID;
- Episode Title;
- Episode Description; and
- creation time.

Stored full input/output bodies shall remain Recall content rather than List content.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-LIST-FILTERS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Deterministic List Filters
STATEMENT: >>>
The shared memory list operation shall support deterministic metadata filtering sufficient for practical discovery.

Approved filter dimensions include:

- memory or conversation name;
- memory type;
- date range; and
- deterministic description matching.

List shall not silently become semantic full-memory retrieval.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-LIST

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.4. Delete

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-DELETE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Deterministic Memory Delete
STATEMENT: >>>
ghost_memory_delete shall delete individual memory episodes only through an exact selector:

- exact Recall Key; or
- exact Record ID.

Delete shall never use semantic similarity, a natural-language description, Episode Description similarity, vector retrieval, fuzzy matching, or an LLM decision to choose what data to destroy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-DELETE-DUPLICATE-SAFETY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Duplicate Recall-Key Safety
STATEMENT: >>>
If an exact Recall Key resolves to multiple owner-scoped records, GHOST shall not silently choose an arbitrary record for deletion.

The user shall be given deterministic identifiers sufficient to select the intended episode, or shall explicitly request deletion of all exact matches where that behavior is supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-DELETE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-DELETE-NO-CLIPBOARD
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Clipboard Excluded from Generic Delete
STATEMENT: >>>
Clipboard Memory shall not participate in the generic ghost_memory_delete operation.

Clipboard lifecycle shall be controlled by its dedicated short-retention policy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-DELETE

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Episodic Memory

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-ROOT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Episodic Memory Scope
STATEMENT: >>>
Episodic Memory shall store ordinary persistent memory episodes that can later be recovered either:

- directly through an exact Recall Key or Record ID; or
- intelligently from a natural-language description.

Direct Recall and intelligent retrieval shall be two access paths to the same Episodic Memory rather than separate memory types.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-DESCRIPTION-REQUIRED
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Episode Description Required for Episodic Save
STATEMENT: >>>
Each newly saved Episodic Memory episode shall contain a non-empty Episode Description.

The description shall summarize the semantic content or useful meaning of that individual episode sufficiently to support later intelligent retrieval.

The Episode Description shall not be replaced by the Episode Title.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-DESCRIPTION-VECTOR
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Episode Description Embedding
STATEMENT: >>>
The Episode Description shall have a precomputed vector representation available for intelligent Episodic retrieval.

The description embedding shall be created from the stored Episode Description rather than generated dynamically from the complete episode during every recall.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-DESCRIPTION-REQUIRED

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-INTELLIGENT-QUERY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Intelligent Recall Query Description
STATEMENT: >>>
When the user requests a memory without knowing an exact identifier, ChatGPT shall formulate the semantic description of the memory being sought.

That query description shall be embedded at recall time and compared against stored Episode Description embeddings.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-DATE-NARROWING
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Optional Date Narrowing
STATEMENT: >>>
Intelligent Episodic retrieval may first apply a deterministic SQL date-range filter when the user's request provides a relevant date or date interval.

Date range is the approved deterministic narrowing dimension for the intelligent Episodic retrieval path.

The intelligent path shall not invent key-prefix, title-prefix, or approximate Recall Key filtering as additional narrowing mechanisms.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-INTELLIGENT-QUERY

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-COSINE-RANKING
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Episode Description Similarity Ranking
STATEMENT: >>>
After any optional date narrowing, intelligent Episodic retrieval shall compare the query-description vector with stored Episode Description vectors using cosine similarity or the equivalent cosine-ranking behavior of the selected vector implementation.

Ranking shall be based primarily on Episode Description semantics.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-INTELLIGENT-QUERY

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-CANDIDATE-RETURN
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Compact Intelligent Recall Candidates
STATEMENT: >>>
The intelligent retrieval stage shall return only a small ranked candidate set to the client model.

The target candidate set shall normally contain approximately five to ten candidates.

Each candidate shall provide sufficient metadata for selection, including at least:

- Record ID; and
- Episode Description.

The candidate stage shall not return the complete stored Q/A bodies for every candidate.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-COSINE-RANKING

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-CLIENT-SELECTION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Client Model Candidate Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
After receiving the compact ranked candidate descriptions, the invoking AI client may use the user's request and candidate descriptions to select the intended episode.

The selection result shall resolve to an exact Record ID before the full episode is fetched.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-CANDIDATE-RETURN

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-EXACT-FINAL-FETCH
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact Final Episode Fetch
STATEMENT: >>>
After intelligent candidate selection, GHOST shall fetch the chosen full episode deterministically by exact Record ID.

Full episode content shall be loaded only after the candidate-selection step has resolved the exact stored record.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-CLIENT-SELECTION

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-NO-TITLE-FIRST-FUNNEL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: No Mandatory Title-First Semantic Funnel
STATEMENT: >>>
Episode Title shall remain useful human-facing metadata but shall not be a mandatory first semantic-ranking stage before Episode Description similarity.

The approved intelligent-retrieval path shall rank Episode Descriptions directly.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EPISODIC-COSINE-RANKING

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Clipboard Memory

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Clipboard Memory Scope
STATEMENT: >>>
Clipboard Memory shall provide short-lived, deterministic temporary memory slots for lightweight save-and-recall workflows.

Clipboard Memory shall use the reserved slot identifiers:

M1 through M100.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-RESERVED-KEYS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Reserved Clipboard Routing
STATEMENT: >>>
M1 through M100 shall be reserved for Clipboard Memory.

A normal Episodic save shall not silently store an M1-M100 key as an ordinary Episodic Recall Key.

When a user explicitly requests saving to or recalling from M1-M100, the request shall be routed to Clipboard Memory behavior.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-DAILY-FILE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: One Clipboard File Per Day
STATEMENT: >>>
For each authenticated owner, Clipboard Memory shall use at most one Clipboard memory history file for a UTC day in which Clipboard content is saved.

Clipboard storage shall not perform intra-day file rollover merely because several Clipboard episodes are appended.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-APPEND-ONLY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Append-Only Clipboard Storage
STATEMENT: >>>
Clipboard writes shall be append-only.

Saving to an already used slot shall append a new episode with the same slot identifier rather than physically overwriting the older episode.

For example, repeated saves to M7 may produce several historical M7 episodes in durable storage.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-LATEST-RECALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Newest Matching Clipboard Recall
STATEMENT: >>>
Recall of a Clipboard slot shall return the newest owner-scoped episode with that exact slot identifier.

Creation timestamps and deterministic ordering metadata shall be sufficient to identify the newest matching episode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-APPEND-ONLY

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-CONTENT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Clipboard Episode Content
STATEMENT: >>>
A Clipboard episode shall store the visible saved content required by the operation and shall also contain an Episode Description.

Clipboard episodes shall not maintain an ActiveBrief.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-NO-SEMANTIC-RETRIEVAL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Clipboard Uses Exact Slot Recall Only
STATEMENT: >>>
Clipboard Memory shall not provide intelligent semantic retrieval.

Clipboard Recall shall use the exact M1-M100 slot identifier and return the newest exact match.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-NO-GENERIC-LIST-DELETE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Clipboard Outside Generic List and Delete
STATEMENT: >>>
Clipboard Memory shall not participate in the shared generic memory List or Delete operations.

The user-facing model shall treat Clipboard as a temporary slot mechanism rather than as a manually administered long-term memory archive.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-RETENTION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Short Clipboard Retention
STATEMENT: >>>
Clipboard Memory shall be short-lived.

The approved default retention window shall be approximately ten days, represented through explicit expiration metadata rather than inferred from a filename.

Expired Clipboard histories shall be eligible for physical deletion together with their corresponding SQLite index rows.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-STARTUP-CLEANUP
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Asynchronous Expired Clipboard Cleanup
STATEMENT: >>>
Expired Clipboard memory cleanup shall run asynchronously during MCP/server startup.

Startup cleanup shall use authoritative expiration metadata and shall remove expired durable Clipboard files and corresponding index records coherently.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIPBOARD-RETENTION

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. Collection Memory

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Collection Memory Scope
STATEMENT: >>>
Collection Memory shall provide a persistent topic-oriented container into which explicitly requested memory episodes can be appended over time.

A Collection is not an automatically recorded conversation.

A Collection groups intentionally saved episodes around a user-defined subject or purpose.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-MODEL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-INIT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Collection Initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
Creating a Collection shall require:

- Collection Name; and
- Collection Description or Purpose.

Initialization shall create a stable Collection identity and shall record its creation time.

The underlying stable file_id shall serve as the Collection ID.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-IDENTITY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Stable Collection Identity
STATEMENT: >>>
Collection ID shall remain stable independently of later episode appends.

A Collection may be targeted for an append by:

- exact Collection ID; or
- exact Collection Name where that name resolves safely within the authenticated owner's scope.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-INIT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-EXPLICIT-APPEND
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Collection Append Is Explicit
STATEMENT: >>>
A Collection shall receive a new episode only when the user explicitly asks GHOST to save or add content to that Collection.

Normal conversation turns shall not be appended automatically merely because a Collection exists.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-EPISODE-METADATA
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Collection Episode Description
STATEMENT: >>>
Every appended Collection episode shall contain an Episode Description describing that episode's local contribution to the Collection.

A Recall Key may be explicitly supplied or generated according to the shared Save policy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-EXPLICIT-APPEND

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ACTIVEBRIEF
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Collection Cumulative ActiveBrief
STATEMENT: >>>
Every appended Collection episode shall also carry the current cumulative Collection ActiveBrief.

The Collection ActiveBrief shall summarize the accumulated knowledge or state of the Collection's fixed topic after incorporating the new episode.

The Collection ActiveBrief is not a conversation-summary mechanism and shall not be confused with ActiveBlackboard merely because both use an ActiveBrief concept.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-EXPLICIT-APPEND

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-LIST
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: List Collections
STATEMENT: >>>
GHOST shall support listing Collections for the authenticated owner.

The Collection list shall provide sufficient metadata for deterministic identification, including at least:

- Collection ID;
- Collection Name;
- Collection Description or Purpose; and
- creation date.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-LIST-EPISODES
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: List Episodes in a Collection
STATEMENT: >>>
Given an exact Collection ID, GHOST shall support listing the episodes belonging to that Collection.

The episode list shall return metadata for all Collection episodes, including:

- Recall Key where present; and
- Episode Description.

This operation is metadata navigation and shall not automatically return the complete stored content of every episode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-LIST

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-INDIVIDUAL-RECALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Individual Collection Episode Recall
STATEMENT: >>>
An individual Collection episode shall not require a separate Collection-specific recall mechanism when it has an exact Recall Key or Record ID.

The shared exact Recall capability shall be used for an individual episode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-RANGE-RECALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Collection Episode Range Recall
STATEMENT: >>>
GHOST shall support Collection-specific retrieval by episode number or episode range.

Examples include:

- one episode such as episode 3; or
- a range such as episodes 2 through 7.

Episode ordering shall be deterministic within the Collection.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-RANGE-TOKEN-SAFETY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Token-Safe Collection Range Recall
STATEMENT: >>>
When a requested Collection range would produce more content than can be returned safely in the active client/model context, GHOST may return a deterministic prefix of the requested range.

The response shall explicitly identify the unreturned remainder so that the client can request it subsequently.

The exact token threshold or page size is intentionally not fixed by this requirement.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-RANGE-RECALL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-DELETE-WHOLE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Whole Collection Delete
STATEMENT: >>>
Deleting an entire Collection shall be a separate destructive operation from deleting an individual memory episode.

Whole-Collection deletion shall require the exact Collection ID.

A Collection shall not be destroyed by semantic description, Collection Name similarity, or LLM selection.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-DELETE-CONFIRMATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Two-Step Whole Collection Delete Safety
STATEMENT: >>>
The first exact request to delete an entire Collection shall not immediately execute the deletion.

GHOST shall return a warning or refusal requiring confirmation.

Only a repeated exact deletion request for the same Collection ID shall authorize the whole-Collection deletion.

The exact implementation of confirmation state, token, timeout, or persistence is intentionally not defined until separately designed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-DELETE-WHOLE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-INDIVIDUAL-DELETE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Individual Collection Episode Delete
STATEMENT: >>>
Deleting an individual episode from a Collection shall use the shared deterministic memory Delete behavior.

No separate Collection-specific single-episode deletion contract is required.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-COLLECTION-ROOT

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 8. Current Implementation and Target Boundary

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The current MCP implementation already provides:

- ghost_engineer_prompt;
- ghost_memory_tag;
- ghost_memory_recall;
- ghost_memory_list; and
- ghost_memory_delete.

The current memory implementation already uses authenticated owner scoping and shared GHOST MemoryRecord/.ragmem/.ragmeta.json/SQLite infrastructure.

The current implementation does not yet constitute the complete approved Episodic intelligent-retrieval, Clipboard, or Collection behavior defined above.

Those requirements describe the approved target behavior and shall not be falsely reported as already complete.

Exact future public tool identifiers for newly implemented Clipboard- and Collection-specific operations are intentionally not invented in this requirement document.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CAP-NO-IMPLEMENTATION-INVENTION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: No False Implementation Claim
STATEMENT: >>>
A requirement in this document shall not be reported as currently implemented solely because underlying data fields or partial infrastructure already exist.

Implementation status shall require corresponding executable behavior and verification.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CAP-ROOT

[[/SECTION]]
